  "contract": "poll(2): a return of 0 means the timeout expired before any descriptor became ready. Linux do_poll rescans descriptors before accepting the timeout.",
  "observed": "poll returns 0 at the timeout boundary although the timerfd was already readable (observed readable while the poller slept), and an immediate nonblocking read returns a full tick.",
